                    <h1 class="entry-title post-title">Company</h1>


                    <div class="post-entry">
                        <h4>About Us</h4>
                        <p>The staff at TTS has been working with the financial industry since 1983. Total Training Solutions has delivered training in many formats from classroom to web-based.</p>
                        <p>We have worked exclusively with the financial industry since our founding. Because of this, we understand the needs of training departments in financial institutions and are alert to changes which affect the industry. We maintain a network of consultants throughout the country who serve as subject matter experts when needed.</p>
                        <h1>Our Staff</h1>
                        <div id="staff-pod">
                            <div id="staff-image"><img src="http://ttstrain.com/wp-content/plugins/lazy-load/images/1x1.trans.gif" data-lazy-src="http://ttstrain.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/Mark-e1462291768452.jpg" class="Yes" alt="Mark Bennett"><noscript><img class="Yes" src="http://ttstrain.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/Mark-e1462291768452.jpg" alt="Mark Bennett" /></noscript></div>

                            <div id="staff-bio">
                                <div><h3>Mark Bennett</h3></div>
                                <div><h5>President</h5></div>
                                <div><a href="mailto:Mark@ttsTrain.com">Mark@ttsTrain.com</a> | <a href="tel:800-831-0678x704">800-831-0678x704</a></div>
                                <div>
                                    <p><p>Mark has been involved in bank training his entire career.   He began in a holding company in Southwestern Wisconsin.  From there, he traveled the country conducting live seminars for state banking associations.   Mark produced dozens of bank training videos and oversaw the transition from video to CD-Rom to Self Paced Online Training.  In 2003 Mark introduced webinars to the banking industry.  Since that time, TTS has gone on to produce thousands of webinars.   Mark received a BBA degree from the University of Wisconsin – Whitewater.  He also is a graduate of the Bank Marketing School in Boulder, Colorado.   Mark resides in Waunakee, WI.</p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div><div id="staff-pod">
                            <div id="staff-image"><img src="http://ttstrain.com/wp-content/plugins/lazy-load/images/1x1.trans.gif" data-lazy-src="http://ttstrain.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/04/Screen-Shot-2016-04-19-at-2.12.01-PM.png" class="Yes" alt="Kyle Bennett"><noscript><img class="Yes" src="http://ttstrain.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/04/Screen-Shot-2016-04-19-at-2.12.01-PM.png" alt="Kyle Bennett" /></noscript></div>

                            <div id="staff-bio">
                                <div><h3>Kyle Bennett</h3></div>
                                <div><h5>Sr. Vice President</h5></div>
                                <div><a href="mailto:kyle@ttsTrain.com">kyle@ttsTrain.com</a> | <a href="tel:800-831-0678x708">800-831-0678x708</a></div>
                                <div>
                                    <p><p>Kyle is a 2004 graduate of the University of Wisconsin-Madison.  His career in the financial industry started as a Management Trainee with First American Bank in Illinois.  Kyle then joined TTS in 2006 and his role has expanded from &#8220;Email Marketer&#8221; to overseer of all day-to-day functions within the organization.  Kyle currently resides in Mt. Prospect, Illinois.</p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div><div id="staff-pod">
                            <div id="staff-image"><img src="http://ttstrain.com/wp-content/plugins/lazy-load/images/1x1.trans.gif" data-lazy-src="http://ttstrain.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/Wesley-Blue-e1462291712532.jpg" class="Yes" alt="Wesley Kavelaris"><noscript><img class="Yes" src="http://ttstrain.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/Wesley-Blue-e1462291712532.jpg" alt="Wesley Kavelaris" /></noscript></div>

                            <div id="staff-bio">
                                <div><h3>Wesley Kavelaris</h3></div>
                                <div><h5>Product Manager</h5></div>
                                <div><a href="mailto:Wesley@ttsTrain.com">Wesley@ttsTrain.com</a> | <a href="tel:800-831-0678x703">800-831-0678x703</a></div>
                                <div>
                                    <p><p>Wesley joined TTS in 2013 as Product Manager. Initially responsible for The Directors Education Series and TTS’s Conference Streaming and Video Archiving services as well as Customer Service, his role has expanded to include the launch and oversight of CUWebinars.com. A lifelong Wisconsinite and graduate of the University of Wisconsin &#8211; Madison, Wesley enjoys the many outdoor sporting activities Wisconsin offers year-round. An avid hobbyist, Wesley is also a bee keeper, gardener and yoga instructor. </p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div><div id="staff-pod">
                            <div id="staff-image"><img src="http://ttstrain.com/wp-content/plugins/lazy-load/images/1x1.trans.gif" data-lazy-src="http://ttstrain.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/Dan.jpg" class="Yes" alt="Dan Heldmann"><noscript><img class="Yes" src="http://ttstrain.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/Dan.jpg" alt="Dan Heldmann" /></noscript></div>

                            <div id="staff-bio">
                                <div><h3>Dan Heldmann</h3></div>
                                <div><h5>Business Development Manager</h5></div>
                                <div><a href="mailto:Dan@ttsTrain.com">Dan@ttsTrain.com</a> | <a href="tel:800-831-0678x705">800-831-0678x705</a></div>
                                <div>
                                    <p><p>Dan joined TTS in 2015 as the Business Development Manager. His responsibilities include working with partner affiliates, email marketing, and in general making sure TTS provides the very best content to its customers. A lifelong Wisconsinite and graduate of the University of Wisconsin – Stevens Point, Dan enjoys spending time with his wife and two young boys. As a sports enthusiast, Dan enjoys playing golf and attending live sporting events. Dan resides in Sun Prairie, WI.</p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div><div id="staff-pod">
                            <div id="staff-image"><img src="http://ttstrain.com/wp-content/plugins/lazy-load/images/1x1.trans.gif" data-lazy-src="http://ttstrain.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Steve-1.jpg" class="Yes" alt="Steve Hueners"><noscript><img class="Yes" src="http://ttstrain.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Steve-1.jpg" alt="Steve Hueners" /></noscript></div>

                            <div id="staff-bio">
                                <div><h3>Steve Hueners</h3></div>
                                <div><h5>Developer</h5></div>
                                <div><a href="mailto:steve@ttstrain.com">steve@ttstrain.com</a> | <a href="tel:800-831-0678 ext 7">800-831-0678 ext 7</a></div>
                                <div>
                                    <p><p>
                                        Steve began a life-long computer career in the late 1980s when Desktop Publishing was &#8216;a thing&#8217;. He was an early adopter of online publishing and has been involved in web-based instructional systems since 1995.<br />
                                        He has lived in the midwest throughout that career and currently lives in the scenic Mississippi River valley near LaCrosse Wisconin.
                                    </p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div><div id="staff-pod">
                            <div id="staff-image"><img src="http://ttstrain.com/wp-content/plugins/lazy-load/images/1x1.trans.gif" data-lazy-src="http://ttstrain.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/Jen.jpg" class="Yes" alt="Jennifer Stewart"><noscript><img class="Yes" src="http://ttstrain.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/Jen.jpg" alt="Jennifer Stewart" /></noscript></div>

                            <div id="staff-bio">
                                <div><h3>Jennifer Stewart</h3></div>
                                <div><h5>Bookkeeper</h5></div>
